WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.669
-Guys, it is time to kick off
the first ever

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.704
"Tonight Show" film festival.
Here we go!

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:06.839
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.642
-"Tonight Show Film Festival."

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.545
-I'm super excited about this.
We teamed up with Samsung

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.749
to find some of the best
rising creators out there.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.283
We got a ton of submissions

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.319
and narrowed them
down to 10 finalists

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.921
and gave each of them
a new Samsung Galaxy

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:26.592
S21 Ultra 5G phone.
There you go right there.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.862
And we asked them to use it
to make a short film for us

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.932
based on the theme,
"A Different Focus."

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.134
This phone, by the way,
is unbelievable.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.236
It's got 8K video.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:40.439
That's, like, the highest
quality available on any phone.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.575
It's got a really cool
director mode feature.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.909
Can you just see
all those lenses

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:45.778
on this back?
Look at that thing.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.446
So, the director mode,
if you do that,

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:48.581
you can just, like, bleep blurp

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.083
through all the different
cameras and stuff.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.153
You could really make
a movie on this thing.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.855
And every night this week,
we're going to air a short film

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.457
created by one of our finalists

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:00.092
using this phone
starting right now.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.894
Tonight's film was created

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:06.299
by Pete Scalzitti,
from Rockport, Texas.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.833
They've been hit hard
by the storms down there,

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.770
and Pete made this film
in the middle of it all.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.072
No running water.
Everything was shut down.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.809
His wife actually had to go
and get the props

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.710
because nothing arrived
in the mail,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.446
and everything broke,
apparently.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:24.050
But he used it and made it part
of his film, and we loved it.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.585
That's one of the reasons
why we loved it.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:29.388
So here it is, the debut of
"Moon Dog," by Pete Scalzitti.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:30.923
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:40.933
♪♪

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.736
[ Dog grumbling ]

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:50.142
♪♪

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.978
[ Reverse signal beeping ]

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.080
♪♪

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.116 line:0%
[ Barking ]

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:04.724
♪♪

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.827
[ Dog growling ]

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.996
[ Sad music plays ]

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:16.802
♪♪

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.406
[ Inspirational music plays ]

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.575
♪♪

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:27.179
[ Grinding ]

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:29.181
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:34.053
♪♪

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:38.357
[ Triumphant music plays ]

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:39.392
[ Dog barks ]

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Dog grumbles ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:45.732
♪♪

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.066
-Tonight's film was created

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:50.770
by Shady Mawajdeh,
from Valrico, Florida.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.672
He's always loved films
and making films,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.942
and his hope is to inspire
others with the work he creates.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.677
He says the film
we're about to see tonight

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.846
is about a man
who has the entire world

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:04.550
as his stage for one minute,
but he doesn't know what to say.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.085
So he says everything.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.421
Here is the debut of
"American Made,"

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.523
by Shady Mawajdeh.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.024
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:22.034
♪♪

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:25.371
-Ladies and gentlemen,
"American Made."

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.239
[ Applause ]

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:30.976
[ Piano playing ]

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.412
My parents came
into this country

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.448
to make a change
with the change that they had.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:39.085
I am the son of success,
so for me, it was never bad.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.954
I'm on "Fallon," Mama.
The world is my stage.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:46.158
I don't know what to say,
but it moves with or without me.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.394
I've been dreaming of this
all my life.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.596
I'm feeling like I'm slipping
through the cracks.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.798
The second hand
is about to hit the minute.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.733
This is the real game,
not the scrimmage.

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:57.570
So let me say this
before I hit my limit.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.705
I am...

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:03.576
Arab American,
American born,

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.612
born and raised in the U.S.A.,

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.547
a child of immigrants,

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:11.183
immigrants who became citizens.

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:14.153
American made.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:20.159
♪♪

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:26.766
♪♪

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.935
-Tonight's film was created
by Margo Akopov.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:33.072
She is a college student,
from Burbank, California.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.074
When her campus shut down
because of COVID-19,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:38.577
she was upset about missing
her senior year, understandably,

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.346
and having to move back home.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:43.582
But she decided to focus
on the positive --

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:45.118
that she was safe
and she was healthy

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.619
and she was with her loved ones.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.088
So with this film, she wants
to challenge everyone to think

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.891
of something positive
that's come from the past year.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.793
Here's the debut of
"Over the Hills and Far Away,"

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:57.463
by Margo Akopov.
[ Applause ]

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:07.472
♪♪

00:05:07.472 --> 00:05:10.576
[ Piano plays ]

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:20.586
♪♪

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:30.596
♪♪

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:40.606
♪♪

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:50.616
♪♪

00:05:50.616 --> 00:06:00.626
♪♪

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:10.636
♪♪

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.538
♪♪

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.307
Tonight's film was created
by Michael Hopkins,

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.143
who lives in Sedona, Arizona.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:20.212
He loves movies
and stop-motion animation.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:24.316
And he says if he can make you
laugh or cry or both,

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.085
then he's done his job.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.955
The film was inspired
by growing up with his dad,

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.922
and it's about taking the time
to pay attention

00:06:30.922 --> 00:06:32.724
to the ones you love.

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:35.995
Here's the debut of "Dear Dad,"
by Michael Hopkins.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.029
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:47.039
♪♪

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:50.042
[ Guitar plays ]

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:58.117
♪♪

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:02.354
[ Keys clacking ]

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:05.257
♪♪

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.259
[ Telephone rings ]

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:10.629
♪♪

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:13.132
[ Keys clacking ]

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:20.606
♪♪

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.709
[ Dog trills ]

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:32.985
♪♪

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:34.720
[ Button clicks,
motor whirring ]

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.056
[ Dog barks ]

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:40.092
[ Birds chirping ]

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:52.038
♪♪

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.073
Now it's time
to show our last film.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.408
It was created
by Whit B. Lauren.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:58.143
She lives
in Southern California.

00:07:58.143 --> 00:08:00.546
She's been creating films
ever since she was a little kid,

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.314
especially science fiction.

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:04.283
Obviously, we're in quarantine,
so she made

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:06.185
this whole film in her garage.

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.419
Super impressive.

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:10.489
Here is the debut of "Prophecy,"
by Whit B. Lauren.

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:11.657
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:21.667
♪♪

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.769
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:26.272
[ Coughing, clock ticking ]

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:28.274
[ Gasps ]

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:32.578
♪♪

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:36.348
-I know you don't remember
recording this video.

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:39.518
Defying time
at accelerated speeds

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:42.188
has a way of warping your brain.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:45.991
And I needed you to remember
why you were there.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:50.162
Welcome to time travel.
This is how you got there,

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:52.998
and this is
how you're going to get back.

00:08:52.998 --> 00:08:57.469
Now I need you to focus,
because you aren't in the past.

00:08:57.469 --> 00:08:59.105
You're in the future.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:03.642
I had a dream about something
that could happen,

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:06.478
and I needed to see
if it's true.

00:09:06.478 --> 00:09:10.049
You are in the year 2026.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:13.919
You need to observe,
and you need to record.

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:17.889
And if what I dreamt is true...

00:09:17.889 --> 00:09:21.160
you need to come back
and warn everyone.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:26.365
♪♪

